From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:50:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [ppc64] runtime: TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 arms, GN wiring, code
 patterns

- runtime/BUILD.gn dart_arch_config: dart_target_arch "ppc64" defines
  TARGET_ARCH_PPC64.
- compiler_sources.gni, vm_sources.gni: the ppc64 files. The assembler and
  IL file sets are generated blocks ("ppc64-sync"), maintained by
  work/dart-ppc64-sync.sh, because those components split their files.
- Arch dispatch: assembler.h, constants.h, cpu.h, instructions.h,
  stack_frame.h, locations_helpers.h.
- vm/globals.h: ppc64 uses the object pool (PP = r30, untagged) and supports
  precompilation.
- assembler_base.cc: the DEBUG code buffer is filled with trap words, not a
  byte memset of the instruction (a non-trapping tdi sled on ppc64).
- ELF: EM_PPC64 (21) with e_flags EF_PPC64_ABI_V2 in the snapshot writer and
  the loader; .cfi for assembly snapshots (CFA = r31 + 16, LR at -8).
- Snapshot features " ppc64"; text padding with trap words; disassembly to
  memory carries the encodings; object pool dump with an untagged PP;
  ReturnAddressLocator; unit-test code runs natively; offsets extractor
  "ppc64"; cpu_test; Float32x4/Float64x2 clamp in portable C.
- instructions_ppc64.{h,cc}: the call and pool-load patterns of ABI-SPEC
  4.1/6.2 (JIT and AOT calls through the pool, IC/switchable calls over two
  consecutive slots, native calls), PC-relative bl/b, the position-
  independent 32-byte far trampoline of ABI-SPEC 4.4, the TTS call, and
  DecodeLoadObjectFromPoolOrThread. BareSwitchableCallPattern is
  UNIMPLEMENTED until the AOT switchable call exists.
- code_patcher_ppc64.cc: pool-slot patching only (ARM64's, with the ppc64
  pool-call decoder). debugger_ppc64.cc: ARM64's (architecture-neutral).
- asm_intrinsifier_ppc64.cc: no assembly intrinsics in v1; every generator
  emits nothing (= not intrinsified).
